app bigint-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "std-bigint — exact non-negative integers of any size as little-endian limb arrays in base 2^24, over array/*, math/* and bytes/*. Base 2^24 because a limb product is below 2^48 and the schoolbook columns split into low and high 24-bit halves whose sums stay below 2^53, so every f64 step is exact; 24 bits is also three whole bytes, so bytes map to limbs with no bit shifting. A number is normalized: every limb a whole number in 0..16777215, the last (highest) limb nonzero, zero is the empty array. FROM_BYTES { data } decodes big-endian padded base64. TO_BYTES { value, size? } encodes big-endian base64, minimal (one 0 byte for zero) or left-padded to size bytes. COMPARE { a, b } answers -1, 0 or 1. ADD, SUB (a >= b), MUL { a, b } answer value. DIVMOD { a, b } answers quotient and remainder by schoolbook long division: each quotient limb is a float estimate from the top three dividend limbs over the top two divisor limbs plus one (never above the true digit, short by at most 3), then corrective subtractions of the divisor until the remainder is below it. MOD { a, b } answers the remainder. MODPOW { a, e, m } answers a^e mod m by left-to-right square-and-multiply from the top set bit of e. MODINV { a, m } answers the inverse of a mod m by the extended Euclid algorithm over unsigned values, refusing no-inverse when gcd(a, m) is not 1. BIGINT_REFUSED { operation, reason } with reason invalid, negative, zero-divisor, zero-modulus, modulus (m not above 1), size or no-inverse. Golden vectors (python3): [5] ^ [117] mod [1000003] is pow(5,117,1000003) = 80309; 3^-1 mod 7 is 5; 2^255-19 is the modulus of the 250-bit inverse probe; every 2048-bit ADD, SUB, MUL, DIVMOD, MOD, MODPOW and MODINV probe matches python's int arithmetic. MUL, DIVMOD and MOD run on engine events (MUL_RUN, DIV_RUN) reached through the ret register; MODPOW and MODINV are each one bounded array/reduce inside a single event (bits of e from the top set bit; at most ceil(1.4405 * bits) + 2 Euclid steps), so they never cascade."
]

orbital BigIntSpec {
  expects entity BigIntRun [runtime] {
    id : string!
  }
  expects trait BigIntCodec {
    state idle {
      FROM_BYTES -> idle
      TO_BYTES -> idle
      ADD -> idle
      SUB -> idle
      MUL -> idle
      COMPARE -> idle
      DIVMOD -> idle
      MOD -> idle
      MODPOW -> idle
      MODINV -> idle
    }
    emits {
      FROM_BYTES_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      TO_BYTES_ANSWERED { value : bytes! }
      ADD_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      SUB_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      MUL_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      COMPARE_ANSWERED { value : number! }
      DIVMOD_ANSWERED { quotient : [number]!  remainder : [number]! }
      MOD_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      MODPOW_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      MODINV_ANSWERED { value : [number]! }
      BIGINT_REFUSED { operation : string!  reason : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page "/bigint" -> BigIntCodec
}
